        "message": "Peladn failed 3 consecutive health checks (~30 min unreachable at https://192.168.4.150:8006).\n\nIf you have CONFIRMED Peladn is really down, trigger failover to Evo-X2:\n\n  curl -sS -u 'n8n:<PASSWORD>' -X POST https://n8n.dkghar.duckdns.org/webhook/peladn-failover\n\nPassword: Vaultwarden -> \"Failover n8n Webhook credentials\" (username: n8n).\nVaultwarden runs on Peladn, so use your OFFLINE vault (phone/desktop app).\n\nOr trigger by hand in n8n:\n  https://n8n.dkghar.duckdns.org/workflow/j4GQTKqjKS9EJGQD\n\nA plain browser click will NOT work (webhook is POST + Basic Auth) — use the curl above.\n\nWhat failover does: restores VM 201 (Talos control plane) + CT 203 (home-ops)\n+ CT 202 (media-ai) from pbs-local on Evo-X2 and starts them. It auto-ABORTS if\nPeladn's API still answers (blip guard); override only with FORCE=1.\n\nDo NOT trigger on a suspected network blip — verify Peladn directly first\n(Proxmox UI / ssh root@192.168.4.150 / ping).",
